0.5.0  2026-11-25
    - a download that fails at its own address is fetched from CKAN's
      copy on archive.org (the checksum decides, as always)
    - fixed: with a single download address, the other strings of the
      metadata were tried as addresses too (so the error named
      "netkan")
    - compat VERSION...: other game versions whose mods count as
      fitting, as CKAN's "compatible game versions" (1.12 is every
      1.12.x); kept per game.  modlist import says which ones a CKAN
      pack was made for.
    - modlist install leaves out (and names) the mods that cannot go
      in, and installs the rest, instead of stopping
    - a mod that clashes with one already chosen is no choice for a
      dependency several provide; conflicts now name both mods
    - the cache keeps each download once, under its checksum (mods
      that share a zip no longer download it again); clean removes
      every archive there, old names too; a download kept under its
      old name is taken over, not fetched again
    - tests/modlist.sh checks them

0.4.0  2026-11-25
    - mods already in the game are found and marked "found" (f in the
      full screen mode, (found) in list, search is:found): what CKAN
      installed, from CKAN/registry.json, and what was put in by hand,
      matched against the module list (version from a file name or a
      .version file, else ?).  On its own when GameData or CKAN's
      registry changed; kspkan scan by hand.  The DLCs and directories
      the module list does not know (Principia) are named, never
      touched.
    - tests/modlist.sh checks it

0.3.2  2026-11-25
    - a dependency that several mods provide (ClassicStockResources-
      PlayMode, Kerbalism-Config, RSSTextures) no longer stops an
      install on a terminal: kspkan lists the choices and asks which,
      once.  A mod in the modlist or on the command line still wins
      without asking; with -y or no terminal it stops and names them.

0.3.1  2026-11-25
    - modlist show, install, pin and sync (and o in the full screen
      mode) take a file when the name is not a saved modlist:
      "kspkan modlist install spelf.ckan" in the directory of the file
      works.  A file CKAN wrote is kept as a modlist named after it
      first; a plain list is used as it is.
    - tests/modlist.sh checks it

0.3.0  2026-11-25
    - modlist import FILE [NAME], and O in the full screen mode: read a
      list CKAN wrote into a kspkan modlist.  It reads .ckan modpacks
      (depends, recommends, the first of any_of), CKAN/registry.json
      (without what CKAN installed as dependencies), the mod lists CKAN
      saves (plain text, Markdown, BBCode, CSV, TSV) and the output of
      "ckan list".  Only reading: nothing is written in CKAN's formats,
      and no JSON is kept.
    - modlists may name a mod without a version (newest that fits)
    - update FILE reads a CKAN-meta .tar.gz you fetched yourself (over
      Tor, on another computer), instead of downloading it
    - fixed: a dependency that several mods provide (FAR, for one) was
      refused even when only one of them fits the game; now only the
      ones that fit count, one you name on the command line wins, and
      the message lists the choices
    - fixed: search cut long ids at 30 letters, so two could look the
      same
    - tests/modlist.sh checks every import format

0.2.0  2026-11-24
    - installed mods are told apart: chosen by you (i) or installed as a
      dependency (d); list, show and the full screen mode say which mods
      need each one, and point out dependencies nothing needs
    - search: is:chosen, is:dep, is:needed, is:orphan
    - full screen mode: i / I go through all, installed, chosen,
      dependencies, unneeded dependencies, not installed, updates, marked
    - full screen mode: p puts the description at the bottom, on the
      right (everything about the mod, scrolled with J K) or off;
      remembered in "settings"
    - modlists: save, show, install, pin, sync, delete; w and o in the
      full screen mode
    - keep and auto (and e in the full screen mode) change a mod between
      chosen and dependency
    - fixed: a key typed right after Esc was lost
    - help is paged when the terminal is short; S orders backwards,
      C clears all marks, r says how many it marked
    - tests/modlist.sh, which needs no network
    - an upgrade that is refused (a file belongs to another module or
      is in the way) now leaves the old version installed
    - installing a module by name that came in as a dependency keeps
      it as yours, so autoremove no longer deletes it
    - reinstalling a metapackage no longer registers it twice
    - fixed a one-byte overflow reading long names in the module list
    - a broken line in the installed list no longer mixes up files

0.1.0  2026-11-24
    First release.
    - module list from CKAN-meta, with download counts
    - dependencies: depends, any_of, provides, conflicts, version limits,
      DLC detection; recommended and suggested modules offered
    - install rules: find, find_regexp, file, as, filter, filter_regexp,
      include_only, find_matches_files, install_to GameRoot
    - checks SHA-256 or SHA-1 of every download; tries every mirror
    - remove with dependents and orphans; upgrade; pinned versions;
      autoremove; clean
    - remembered game instances, shared module list
    - full screen mode: colours (habamax), search, five orders,
      detail pane, keyboard only
    - safe against path traversal, symlinks and zip bombs
